  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> be <math><mn>2</mn></math> circles externally touching each other at point <math><mi>X</mi></math>. Line segment <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is a direct common tangent to circles&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> at points <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> respectively. Another common tangent to <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> at <math><mi>X</mi></math> intersects line <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> at a point <math><mi>Y</mi></math>. If <math><mi>B</mi><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;units and the radius of <math><mi>P</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;units, then the value of the reciprocal of the radius of the circle <math><mi>Q</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0.09",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi>A</mi><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>Y</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math> (<math><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>Y</mi></math> lies on the radical axis)<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/25_que_math.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 146px;\" /><br />From the figure,<br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></math><br /><br />Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;(given)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>9</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>09</mn></math></p>",
